Circular Ledger uses Tesseract.js and Tesseract language data for optional local OCR.
See their upstream repositories and installed package licenses.

The optional romanization feature uses the universal romanizer software 'uroman'
written by Ulf Hermjakob, USC Information Sciences Institute (2015-2020).
See https://github.com/isi-nlp/uroman/blob/master/LICENSE.txt for its license.

Public circulars are fetched from their original publishers into ignored local
data directories. They are not redistributed as part of this repository.
